build/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
managed_components/
.DS_Store
*.tags
tags

# Host preview tool artefacts. All regenerated by `make run` in ~0.2 s, so there is
# nothing to keep — and while they were tracked, every preview run dirtied the tree
# and adding or renaming a case turned up as noise in an unrelated commit.
# *.ppm matters: that is what the tool actually writes (*.pbm was aspirational).
tools/preview/preview
tools/preview/preview.dSYM/
# NOT path-scoped: running ./tools/preview/preview from the repo root writes its
# renders to the CWD, so seven of them landed in a commit while the ignore rule
# only covered tools/preview/.
*.ppm
*.pbm
*.png

# Per-machine editor/tooling config (absolute paths, serial ports)
.vscode/
.claude/

# NOTE: dependencies.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. The mianesp git deps use
# `version: main`, so committing the lock is what makes builds reproducible;
# `idf.py update-dependencies` is the explicit opt-in to move forward.
